# OpenEVV sound map: Hungarian (eSpeak NG voice urj/hu), spoken by openevv's German module
# with the sounds, the melody and the tones of the language itself.
# Written by engine/accent/mapwriter.py; OpenEvvFrontend reads it, and docs/LANGUAGES.md
# says what each line means. Edit freely: the file is read each time a voice starts.

template dedx
style standard
vowels i I e E a A u U o O y Y oe OE @ aj aw oj a~ E~ o~ oe~ E: R
glides r l j w
schwa @
secondary 2

# the melody: peak; a question that wants yes or no: risefall
accent f0=own range=90 shape=0 accent=26 accent2=12 unstressed=-6 decl=8 declmax=30 fs=-18 fw=-12 fc=10 fe=-12 fq=34 qreg=8 span=2 qfall=50 stressed=88 weak=112 last=88 stop=1

# the words a question is asked with, which is not the question that wants yes or no
whwords first ki mi hol mikor hogyan miért melyik mennyi
whwords first hány hová hova honnan milyen mit kit kinek

# what the module says in place of a phone it is given
says C t S
says J d Z
says P p f
says T t s

# the sounds of the language that the module has not, each as it differs from the phone
